  "findings": [
    "The FONTDATA directory records LATINFONT.BIN with short alias LATINF~6.BIN and a declared size of 130886 bytes. The FAT16 reader follows its file chain and checks the terminal marker. The recorded span and hash identify the entire file.",
    "The native DirectLoadFontEx call uses A:\\FontData\\LatinFont.bin. AppResourceGetPath selects media argument 2 and passes the normalized path to original GdiCreateFont. The modeled FileX stat and read supply the exact verified extent. Native code chooses type 0x202, relocates its internal offsets, and selects the original font operations table at 0x80236538. The native static-table size remains zero.",
    "The direct fixture supplies unit 84. The staged fixture supplies default buffer ID 0, text ID 0xffff, coordinates (96,64), count 4 and flag 1 to AppDBTextOutByBufferID. Its synthetic source has header u16 1, the four recorded units and a terminating u16 zero. Native GdiTextOutDB conversion forwards the same units from its stack to FntDrawTextEx through 0x8022968c.",
    "The renderer uses 64 by 48 cells with 16 source bytes per row. The original halfword byte swap consumes the packed 2-bit values in high-bit-first order. Widths 24, 29, 34 and 29 give successive x positions 96, 120, 149 and 183. The fixture's default context skips code 0 and maps codes 1, 2 and 3 to indices 2, 1 and 3.",
    "The independent packed-byte oracle matches the entire synthetic indexed frame and both eight-byte guards in each case. The two changed-byte counts are 563 and 3346, with exact source coordinates, native call arguments, frame hashes and index histograms recorded below the replay."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The verified FAT extent identifies the file bytes supplied in the model. FileX calls, media lookup, allocation, diagnostic logging and inherited raster setup APIs are modeled. Physical filesystem I/O and camera font initialization are outside scope.",
    "The staged source and layout are controlled inputs tied to previously observed sRGB units. The replay starts at the staged text draw request and covers no native menu event or LCD scanout.",
    "Pixel writes are palette indices in a synthetic frame. Font palette colors on a camera, stretch, clipping, other text orientations and other assets are outside the fixtures.",
    "The decoded descriptor declares an inclusive upper bound 0xaa while this file contains 170 packed cells. The tested units are at most 84. Boundary handling for 0xaa is unresolved."
  ],
